      "id": "wf3-respond-00000000008",
      "name": "Respond"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚠️ CONTRACT: WF3 ↔ Dashboard action (SYSTEM OF RECORD)\n\nThe Reece Dashboard is the system of record. `lib/actions/content.ts → rejectComponent()` is the authoritative writer of a rejection. BEFORE this webhook fires, that action has ALREADY:\n  1. inserted the `fb_post_feedback` row (snapshotting the rejected copy/image),\n  2. flipped the rejected component to `status = 'rejected'`,\n  3. incremented `fb_posts.revision`, and\n  4. set `needs_manual = true` once `revision >= MAX_REGEN_ATTEMPTS`.\n\nTHIS workflow CONSUMES that — it must **NOT** insert feedback again. It reads the\nlatest feedback for the post/component (Get Feedback) + the fb_posts row, regenerates\ncopy and/or image (reusing the kept image when only copy was rejected), and sets the\nregenerated component back to `pending`. If `needs_manual` is already set, it alerts on\nGroupMe and stops.\n\nLogic is now COMPLETE: copy branch (Need Copy?) rebuilds the generator prompt in\nregeneration mode and PATCHes post_body/first_comment + copy_status='pending'; image\nbranch (Need Image?) regenerates via decode→PUT→public-URL and PATCHes image_url +\nimage_status='pending'. For component='both' both run.\n\nPayload: { post_id, component, reason_code, reason_text, rejected_by }.\nThe mirror of this note lives in lib/actions/content.ts (rejectComponent).",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 540
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        -300
      ],
      "id": "wf3-note-000000000009",
      "name": "CONTRACT — read me"
    }
  ],
